# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Environment files (secrets)
.env
.env.*

# Private keys
*.pem
*.key

# TAUSIK project data — all runtime, generated by bootstrap (DB cache, venv,
# keys, receipts, logs). The DURABLE, branch-coupled projection lives in the
# NON-dotted `tausik/` (no leading dot) and is deliberately NOT ignored — it is
# the git-native source of truth guarded by the state round-trip gate
# (state-git-roundtrip-gate). Do not add a bare `tausik/` rule here: that would
# re-hide the very state this project commits on purpose.
.tausik/
.frai/

# RAG index data (local, machine-specific)
.rag/

# Generated IDE directories — bootstrap output, not source
.claude/
.claude-project/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.codex/
.qwen/
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.opencode/

# MCP config — generated by bootstrap with machine-specific paths
.mcp.json
.cursorrules
# opencode.json holds ABSOLUTE interpreter/server paths: OpenCode expands no
# workspace variable, so this file is machine-specific by construction.
opencode.json

# Vendor skills config — user-specific, copied from skills.example.json
skills.json

# Official skills — separate repo (github.com/Kibertum/tausik-skills)
skills-official/

# Databases (other)
*.sqlite

# Logs
*.log

# Temp
temp/
nul

# Backup files
*.bak*
.tausik/*.bak.*

# Archives
*.tar.gz

# Coverage / pytest / linter caches (all regenerable)
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.json
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Review reports
REVIEW-REPORT-*.md

# Scratch next-session prompt (not tracked)
prompt.md

# Presentation decks — build artifacts of a narrative, not source. The story
# they tell lives in README, whats-new and the changelog; a PDF in the tree
# would be a fourth copy of the same claims with no gate keeping it true.
# Presentation and storefront artifacts, assembled locally and published by
# hand elsewhere (GitHub settings, org profile, decks). They are BUILDS of a
# narrative whose source lives in README, whats-new and the changelog — where
# gates keep it true. A copy in the tree would be one more place for the same
# claims to drift, with nothing watching it.
TAUSIK-deck-*.pdf
*-social-preview.png
RENAR-readme-draft.md
TAUSIK-pending-*.md
TAUSIK-report-*.md
TAUSIK-report-*.pdf
TAUSIK-roadmap*.pdf
KIBERTUM-org-profile.md

# Confidential / internal — must NOT ship in the public repo (v151 release-readiness)
docs/audit/
tausik_systemwide_analysis.md
# Research lives in three parallel trees (docs/research/, docs/ru/research/,
# docs/en/research/). The sink rule named only the first, so a note moved into
# the sink of a localised tree stayed tracked — the rule looked applied and was
# not. Match the sink wherever it sits instead of naming one of the three.
docs/**/research/_internal/
